cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "6D Foraging Methodology: Strategic Dimensional Discovery"
message: "If you use this methodology, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shatny
    given-names: Michael
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-2011-3258"
repository-code: "https://github.com/semanticintent/6d-foraging-methodology"
url: "https://6d.semanticintent.dev"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.18209945"
abstract: >-
  The 6D Foraging Methodology is a method for tracing how one event
  spreads across six dimensions of an organization or sector (Customer,
  Employee, Revenue, Regulatory, Quality, Operational), with each dimension
  scored 0-100 from cited evidence and the cascade recorded from its origin
  through each layer. Scoring is defined by the CAL specification. Version
  2.0.0 removes the cost multiplier and cascade probabilities of version
  1.0.0 and adds counted cascade patterns from a public library of
  published case studies.
keywords:
  - strategic analysis
  - cascade analysis
  - business dimensions
  - risk assessment
  - 6D methodology
  - foraging methodology
